<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Cortenuova</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1237</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Cortenuova was fought on 27 November 1237 in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>, when the emperor Frederick II defeated the army of the revived <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombard-league">Lombard League</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>. The Milanese carroccio, the city's battle-wagon, was captured and sent to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> as a trophy. The emperor's demand for unconditional surrender stiffened the cities' resistance, however, and he never broke the league.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-cortenuova.jpg" alt="Battle of Cortenuova" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Giovanni Villani, Nuova Cronica, Chronica, 14. Jahrhundert, Biblioteca Apostolica Vaticana, Rom Cod. Chigi L VIII 296... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Erbeutung_des_Mail%C3%A4nder_Carroccios.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
